---
title: Stuffed Bagels
servings: 4
prepTime: 5 mins
cookTime: 8 mins
Rating: 10/10
description: You can customize these by using different flavored bagels, cream cheese, seasonings, jalapenos, bacon, chocolate, Nutella, or just about anything - go wild!
source: https://kitchenfunwithmy3sons.com/stuffed-bagels/
tags: Bread, Breakfast
---

Preheat the oven to 350°F. 
Line a #baking sheet{} with #parchment paper{}.

Slice down through the top of your @bagels{4}(plain) into 6 pieces but DO NOT cut all the way through the bagel.

In a #small bowl{} mix the @cream cheese{8%ounces}(softened) and @sugar{1/2%tbsp}.
Pipe or spoon the cream cheese into each slice in the bagels.

In a #shallow bowl{} mix the @butter{1/2%cup}(melted), @garlic{2%cloves}(minced), and other seasonings.
Stir in @parmesan cheese{1%tbsp}(grated).

> Other suggested toppings include parsley, italian seasoning, or everything bagel seasoning.
> If using minced garlic from a jar, pour in 2 tsp of the garlic juice into the seasoning mixture.

Brush the butter mixture all over the bagels, or dip the top of the bagels in the bowl.

Bake for ~{8-12%minutes} until the bagels are toasted and the cream cheese melted and the tops are golden.

Serve these warm or room temperature. Store leftovers in an airtight container for up to 3 days.

